{
  "dom_id": "step-q236465",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14165968/assets/fae9ac16ebabea7054903ab75f2305f98c757f8ee7fc4924600774e627ad76b4.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x),$ shown above?$\\,$  The range is $f(x)\\in $\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}.",
  "worked_solution": "We find the ranges of the individual pieces, and then calculate their union:\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in (-3,0]$ is $[-2,0)$\n\n- The range of the branch defined on $x\\in (0,3)$ is $(1,3]$\n\nTherefore, the range of $f(x)$ is $[-2,0)\\cup (1,3].$\n\n**Note:** From the graph, we see that the values $y=0$ and $y=1$ are NOT valid outputs of the function $y=f(x).$ Therefore, we use parentheses $(…)$ instead of brackets $[…]$ at these endpoints.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
